# Line endings that matter.
#
# `docker-entrypoint.sh` is the one that would actually break: a shell script checked out with CRLF
# fails inside a Linux container with `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, which is an obscure error to
# meet for the first time in a deploy log. This machine has `core.autocrlf` active, so without this
# the risk is real rather than theoretical.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
